      "note": "Trimming removes FLEXIBLE residues, which removes cost, but the cost model is not linear in length - WP45's 12-20 kcal/mol was priced for a 20-residue flexible pool, not per residue. So the trim is reported as a FACT (fewer movable residues, all functions preserved) and NOT as a fabricated kcal/mol saving. What it does buy is a smaller construct the same staple can rigidify: a 6-torsion staple over 15 residues constrains a larger FRACTION of the molecule than over 19.",
